  {# Section 2: Essential Storage #}
  <section id="essential" class="scroll-mt-6">
    <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-[#164b70] m-0 border-b border-[#d8e3ea] pb-1 flex items-center justify-between">
      <span>2. Strictly Necessary Technologies (&quot;Always Active&quot;)</span>
      <span class="inline-block bg-[#e8f5e9] border border-[#a5d6a7] text-[#1b5e20] text-[10px] font-bold px-2 py-0.5 select-none uppercase tracking-wide">
        Always Active
      </span>
    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2.5">
      The website uses modern browser local storage (<code class="bg-[#eef3f5] text-[#164b70] px-1 py-0.5 border border-[#cad6de]">localStorage</code>) exclusively for essential user preferences and site functionality:
    </p>
    
    <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto border border-[#b7cbd6] bg-[#f8fbfc]">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
        <thead class="bg-[#e4eef2] border-b border-[#b7cbd6] text-[#164b70]">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-2 font-bold">Key Name</th>
            <th class="p-2 font-bold">Type</th>
            <th class="p-2 font-bold">Purpose</th>
            <th class="p-2 font-bold">Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-[#d8e3ea]">
          <tr>
            <td class="p-2 font-mono font-semibold text-[#164b70]">cookie_consent_preferences</td>
            <td class="p-2">localStorage</td>
            <td class="p-2">Remembers which telemetry services you have allowed or declined so you are not prompted repeatedly.</td>
            <td class="p-2">Persistent</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-2 font-mono font-semibold text-[#164b70]">cookie_consent</td>
            <td class="p-2">localStorage</td>
            <td class="p-2">Stores the overall consent status for Google Tag Manager and Microsoft Clarity integration.</td>
            <td class="p-2">Persistent</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-2 font-mono font-semibold text-[#164b70]">announcement_dismissed</td>
            <td class="p-2">localStorage</td>
            <td class="p-2">Remembers if you dismissed the top announcement banner to prevent visual distraction on future visits.</td>
            <td class="p-2">Persistent</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-3 text-[#485b66]">
      <strong>Why these cannot be disabled:</strong> These items remain strictly inside your browser. They do not track you across other websites, do not send telemetry to third parties, and are technically required to honor your choices (such as remembering your cookie rejection). Under EU/GDPR and ePrivacy standards, strictly necessary storage does not require prior consent.
    </p>
  </section>

  {# Section 3: Optional Telemetry Services #}
  <section id="telemetry" class="scroll-mt-6">
    <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-[#164b70] m-0 border-b border-[#d8e3ea] pb-1">
      3. Optional Telemetry &amp; Analytics (Consent Required)
    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2.5">
      To understand how visitors discover this site and find broken links or formatting issues, two optional measurement services can be toggled on or off:
    </p>

    <div class="mt-3 space-y-3">
      {# Google Analytics #}
      <div class="border border-[#b7cbd6] bg-[#f8fbfc] p-3.5">
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-[#164b70] text-sm m-0">A. Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-[#3b4d57]">
          <strong>Provider:</strong> Google LLC (1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[#3b4d57]">
          <strong>What it measures:</strong> Aggregated page views, general referral sources (e.g. GitHub, Google, direct), device type, and generalized regional location. IP masking is enabled by default.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[#3b4d57]">
          <strong>Consent Mode v2:</strong> This site enforces Google Consent Mode v2. All analytics cookies and storage remain completely disabled (<code class="bg-white px-1 py-0.2 border border-[#cad6de]">analytics_storage: &#39;denied&#39;</code>) until you actively choose &quot;Accept All&quot; or toggle Analytics ON.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-[11px] text-[#485b66]">
          More information: <a class="text-[#064f83] underline hover:text-[#c0392b]" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      {# Microsoft Clarity #}
      <div class="border border-[#b7cbd6] bg-[#f8fbfc] p-3.5">
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-[#164b70] text-sm m-0">B. Microsoft Clarity</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-[#3b4d57]">
          <strong>Provider:</strong> Microsoft Corporation (One Microsoft Way, Redmond, WA 98052, USA).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[#3b4d57]">
          <strong>What it measures:</strong> Anonymous interaction behavior, scroll depth, and aggregated heatmaps to help identify broken layout elements or navigation dead ends.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[#3b4d57]">
          <strong>Privacy Safeguards:</strong> Keystroke masking and sensitive input masking are strictly enabled. Clarity is synchronized with your consent choice and remains disabled if rejected.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-[11px] text-[#485b66]">
          More information: <a class="text-[#064f83] underline hover:text-[#c0392b]" href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

